# shell: desktop
# home: fixture
# The terminal is a terminal, not a transcript: a shell runs on a pty, a
# full-screen program addresses the cursor, and what it draws lands where
# it asked.  less is the check because it uses the three things a toy
# terminal lacks -- cursor addressing, erase, and reverse video.
wait 70
click-window Terminal
wait 6
key s
key e
key q
key space
key 1
key space
key 4
key 0
key space
key >
key space
key /
key t
key m
key p
key /
key t
key r
key k
key _
key t
key e
key r
key m
key _
key l
key i
key n
key e
key s
key .
key t
key x
key t
key Return
wait 40
key l
key e
key s
key s
key space
key /
key t
key m
key p
key /
key t
key r
key k
key _
key t
key e
key r
key m
key _
key l
key i
key n
key e
key s
key .
key t
key x
key t
key Return
wait 70
note the file name sits in a REVERSE VIDEO bar along the bottom
expect-pixel 187 510 000000
note space pages forward through the file
key space
wait 60
note quitting puts the shell back and takes the bar with it
key q
wait 60
expect-pixel 187 510 ffffff
note a row painted at an ABSOLUTE position lands on that row
key s
key h
key space
key /
key t
key m
key p
key /
key t
key r
key k
key _
key t
key e
key r
key m
key _
key c
key u
key p
key .
key s
key h
key Return
wait 60
expect-pixel 500 293 000000
note and nothing above it moved: row 11 is still the shell's own text
expect-pixel 500 275 ffffff
